als from the pancreas travel in the dorsal column?</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>2001</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11166477</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3959(00)00364-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Cui</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Chaer</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Epigastric antinociception by cervical dorsal column lesions in rats</article-title><source>Anesthesiology</source><year>1998</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>411</fpage><lpage>420</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9710400</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00000542-199808000-00018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al-chaer</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Lawand</surname><given-names>NB</given-names></name><name><surname>Westlund</surname><given-names>KN</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Visceral nociceptive input into the ventral posterolateral nucleus of the thalamus: a new function for the dorsal column pathway</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>1996</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>2661</fpage><lpage>2674</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8899636</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al-chaer</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Feng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A role for the dorsal column in nociceptive visceral input into the thalamus of primates</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>1998</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>3143</fpage><lpage>3150</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9636114</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Lin</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lieu</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>CY</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hung</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Loh</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuo</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Howng</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High cervical midline punctate myelotomy in the management of visceral pain in the mouse</article-title><source>Kaohsiung J Med Sci</source><year>2003</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>159</fpage><lpage>162</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12795344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Palecek</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Paleckov</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Willis</surname><given-names>WD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The roles of pathways in the spinal cord lateral and dorsal funiculi in signaling nociceptive somatic and visceral stimuli in rats</article-title><source>Pain</source><year>2002</year><fpage>297</fpage><lpage>307</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11973002</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-3959(01)00459-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation c